<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-introduction" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Introduction: <pretext/> for course materials</title>

<p>
  <pretext/> is an open-source authoring system designed to make it easy to create high-quality, accessible, scholarly documents.  It is a popular choice for authoring OER textbooks, especially in mathematics.  Recent development has made it a lot easier to use <pretext/> for smaller documents, include research articles and course materials.  This book is intended to help instructors get started using <pretext/> to create course materials such as lecture notes, homework sets, and in-class activities.
</p>

<p>
  The introduction of the <url href="https://pretextbook.org/doc/guide/html/start-here.html"><pretext/> guide</url> contains more information about the advantages of philosophy of <pretext/>.
</p>

</chapter>
